# Traits
modifier.crystex_frost.name=Frost
modifier.crystex_frost.desc=§bSlowly freezing...§r\nYour attacks apply Slowness to enemies, as if engulfed by severe cold.

modifier.crystex_catalysis.name=Catalysis
modifier.crystex_catalysis.desc=§9XP Multiplier\n§rMining or attacking has a chance to double the dropped XP orbs. (20% for head, 10% for others)

modifier.crystex_molten_core.name=Molten Core
modifier.crystex_molten_core.desc=§6Molten Core\n§r+45% mining speed, +25% damage, and auto-smelts mined ores. Fails and applies severe penalties in water or rain.

modifier.crystex_heavy_crush.name=Heavy Crush
modifier.crystex_heavy_crush.desc=§8Heavy Crush\n§rProvides extremely high handle modifier. 20% chance to root targets for 2 seconds on hit. Fails in water or rain.

modifier.crystex_hydrolysis.name=Hydrolysis
modifier.crystex_hydrolysis.desc=§9Hydrolysis\n§rFatal weakness. When touching water or in rain, mining speed -70%, damage -50%, and tool rapidly loses durability. Cannot be repaired while hydrolyzed.

effect.tinkerscrystex.root=Root
modifier.crystex_abyssal_pressure.desc=§9Crushing weight of the abyss...§r\nIncreased mining speed and damage while in water. Attacks have a chance to launch enemies and drain their air. Decreased stats on land.

modifier.crystex_unstable.name=Unstable
modifier.crystex_unstable.desc=§cOn the edge of frenzy!§r\nSignificantly increased mining speed and damage when durability is extremely low, but every use has a chance to consume extra durability.

modifier.crystex_briar_sting.name=Briar Sting
modifier.crystex_briar_sting.desc=§2A fatal embrace...§r\nWhen attacked, reflects a percentage of damage back to the attacker and has a chance to inflict poison.

modifier.crystex_aura.name=Aura
modifier.crystex_aura.desc=§3Absorbing the essence...§r\nTools gain significant mining speed and durability regeneration in specific environments (The End or deep underground), with a slight speed boost at night.

modifier.crystex_regrowth.name=Regrowth
modifier.crystex_regrowth.desc=§aEndless vitality.§r\nTools slowly repair themselves when not in use, up to 80% durability.

